    {
      "name": "Test Data Generation",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Notes - How to Test",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": ""
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://localhost:5000",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["localhost"],
              "port": "5000"
            },
            "description": "TESTING INSTRUCTIONS FOR PHASE 1:\n\n1. DATABASE SETUP:\n   - Ensure PostgreSQL is running\n   - Create database: createdb parkit_dev\n   - Enable PostGIS: psql -d parkit_dev -c \"CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS postgis;\"\n   - Set environment variables in .env:\n     DB_NAME=parkit_dev\n     DB_USER=postgres\n     DB_PASSWORD=your_password\n     DB_HOST=localhost\n     DB_PORT=5432\n\n2. SERVER SETUP:\n   - Install dependencies: npm install\n   - Run migrations: npm run migrate (if available)\n   - Start server: npm start\n   - Server should be running on http://localhost:5000\n\n3. INSERT TEST DATA:\n   - You need to insert parking spaces into the database\n   - Use a database tool (pgAdmin, DBeaver) or SQL scripts\n   - Make sure spaces have latitude/longitude values\n   - Ensure location geometry is populated\n   - Set verification_status to 'verified'\n   - Set is_active to true\n   - Set available_slots > 0\n\n4. TEST ENDPOINTS:\n   - Start with \"Search Nearby Spaces - Basic\"\n   - Verify response includes distance_km and relevance_score\n   - Try different sort_by values (distance, rating, price, availability)\n   - Test destination search (requires GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY in .env)\n   - Get space details for an existing space ID\n   - Check trending spaces\n\n5. EXPECTED RESPONSE FORMAT:\n   {\n     \"success\": true,\n     \"data\": [...parking spaces...],\n     \"total\": 15,\n     \"limit\": 20,\n     \"skip\": 0,\n     \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-02T10:30:00Z\"\n   }\n\n6. TROUBLESHOOTING:\n   - If you get \"no results\", check:\n     * Parking spaces exist in database\n     * location geometry is populated\n     * is_active = true\n     * available_slots > 0\n     * verification_status = 'verified'\n   \n   - If geocoding fails:\n     * Check GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY is set\n     * Verify API key has Geocoding API enabled\n     * Use mock data (supported in test mode)\n\n   - Check server logs for detailed error messages"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
